{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794075607936,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b73d392c001ZizhjDCZlc9O5e","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b73c3602001aT5Xegmqr7ovg1","type":"tool","id":"call_bf0250f91d094cf2b5a3d49f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && git diff ac32d66fed..7714ff26b1 -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md | head -260"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\nindex 6164e94cf2..8f9cf58807 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"scratch folder usage\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.6.6.0\n+version: 1.6.7.0\n ---\n \n # Folder Structure Reference\n@@ -94,6 +94,34 @@ Format: `NNN-topic-name`\n └── 003-performance-optimization/\n ```\n \n+### Sub-Track Folders\n+\n+A track may hold one optional level of named sub-tracks between itself and its packets:\n+\n+```\n+specs/<track>/\n+├── <NNN>-<slug>/                  # packet filed directly in the track\n+├── <sub-track>/\n+│   ├── 001-<slug>/                # numbering restarts inside the sub-track\n+│   └── 002-<slug>/\n+└── z_archive/\n+```\n+\n+A sub-track is declared, not inferred. All of these hold:\n+\n+| Part | Requirement |\n+|---|---|\n+| Shape | Direct child of a track root, name not `NNN-*`, no `spec.md` |\n+| `description.json` | `\"level\": \"sub-track\"`, with `specFolder` and `specId` set to `<track>/<sub-track>` |\n+| `graph-metadata.json` | Track-root shape: `packet_id` `<track>/<sub-track>`, `parent_id` the track, `children_ids` its immediate numbered packets |\n+| Track registration | The sub-track id appears in the track's `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` |\n+\n+Numbering continues per folder, so each sub-track numbers its own packets from `001`. One level is supported: a sub-track holds numbered packets, not another sub-track.\n+\n+A track's `children_ids` lists its direct numbered packets and its declared sub-tracks. A sub-track's `children_ids` lists only its own immediate numbered packets. A numbered phase parent counts as one entry, and its phases stay its own children.\n+\n+A sub-track has its own `z_archive/`. Any `z_` folder inside a track or sub-track is never a sub-track and is never discovered as content. A non-numbered folder without the declaration gets one diagnostic and is never promoted. A symlinked sub-track is skipped with one diagnostic in both the working-tree and the commit view. Diagnostics are advisory and never change an exit code.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 3. LEVEL REQUIREMENTS\n@@ -257,6 +285,18 @@ specs/\n     └── 002-abandoned-approach/\n ```\n \n+A declared sub-track archives into its own `z_archive/`, not the track's:\n+\n+```\n+specs/demo/\n+├── sub/\n+│   ├── 001-active/\n+│   └── z_archive/\n+│       └── 001-retired/\n+└── z_archive/\n+    └── 001-old-track-packet/\n+```\n+\n **Archive Triggers:**\n - Feature fully implemented and verified\n - Approach abandoned for alternative\n@@ -337,9 +377,61 @@ specs/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/        <- Coordination root (point-in-time snapshot\n     └── 002-skill-review/            <- Nested child\n ```\n \n+### Track With Sub-Tracks\n+\n+```\n+specs/billing/\n+├── description.json                 # level: \"track\"\n+├── graph-metadata.json              # children_ids: 001-invoices, invoicing\n+├── 001-invoices/\n+│   ├── spec.md\n+│   └── ...\n+├── invoicing/                       # declared sub-track\n+│   ├── description.json             # level: \"sub-track\"\n+│   ├── graph-metadata.json          # parent_id: billing\n+│   ├── 001-numbering/\n+│   │   ├── spec.md\n+│   │   └── ...\n+│   └── 002-credits/\n+└── z_archive/\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. HOST REPOSITORY TRIGGER INDEX\n+\n+The packaged index at `runtime/data/trigger-index.json` is the default every lookup reads. A host repository that vendors Skilled can build an index over its own docs at `.speckit-index/trigger-index.json`. Nothing selects that file on its own, so the host passes it with `--index`.\n+\n+Generate from the host root:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --repo-root . \\\n+  --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+```\n+\n+Call it from the host's Gate 1 lookup:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --index .speckit-index/trigger-index.json \\\n+  --json -- \"<prompt>\"\n+```\n+\n+Exit `0` means candidates, `1` a clean miss and `2` a bad invocation or an unreadable index. `--out` alone writes the corpus manifest, diagnostics and phrase variants beside the index. Check freshness against the same file:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --check \\\n+  --repo-root . \\\n+  --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+```\n+\n+Without `--index`, the lookup keeps reading the packaged index.\n+\n ---\n \n-## 7. RELATED RESOURCES\n+## 8. RELATED RESOURCES\n \n - [spec-kit-docs.json](../../templates/spec-kit-docs.json) - Level contract resolved by create.sh\n - [Template Guide](../templates/template-guide.md)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\nindex 6164e94cf2..8f9cf58807 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md\n@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"scratch folder usage\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.6.6.0\n+version: 1.6.7.0\n ---\n \n # Folder Structure Reference\n@@ -94,6 +94,34 @@ Format: `NNN-topic-name`\n └── 003-performance-optimization/\n ```\n \n+### Sub-Track Folders\n+\n+A track may hold one optional level of named sub-tracks between itself and its packets:\n+\n+```\n+specs/<track>/\n+├── <NNN>-<slug>/                  # packet filed directly in the track\n+├── <sub-track>/\n+│   ├── 001-<slug>/                # numbering restarts inside the sub-track\n+│   └── 002-<slug>/\n+└── z_archive/\n+```\n+\n+A sub-track is declared, not inferred. All of these hold:\n+\n+| Part | Requirement |\n+|---|---|\n+| Shape | Direct child of a track root, name not `NNN-*`, no `spec.md` |\n+| `description.json` | `\"level\": \"sub-track\"`, with `specFolder` and `specId` set to `<track>/<sub-track>` |\n+| `graph-metadata.json` | Track-root shape: `packet_id` `<track>/<sub-track>`, `parent_id` the track, `children_ids` its immediate numbered packets |\n+| Track registration | The sub-track id appears in the track's `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` |\n+\n+Numbering continues per folder, so each sub-track numbers its own packets from `001`. One level is supported: a sub-track holds numbered packets, not another sub-track.\n+\n+A track's `children_ids` lists its direct numbered packets and its declared sub-tracks. A sub-track's `children_ids` lists only its own immediate numbered packets. A numbered phase parent counts as one entry, and its phases stay its own children.\n+\n+A sub-track has its own `z_archive/`. Any `z_` folder inside a track or sub-track is never a sub-track and is never discovered as content. A non-numbered folder without the declaration gets one diagnostic and is never promoted. A symlinked sub-track is skipped with one diagnostic in both the working-tree and the commit view. Diagnostics are advisory and never change an exit code.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 3. LEVEL REQUIREMENTS\n@@ -257,6 +285,18 @@ specs/\n     └── 002-abandoned-approach/\n ```\n \n+A declared sub-track archives into its own `z_archive/`, not the track's:\n+\n+```\n+specs/demo/\n+├── sub/\n+│   ├── 001-active/\n+│   └── z_archive/\n+│       └── 001-retired/\n+└── z_archive/\n+    └── 001-old-track-packet/\n+```\n+\n **Archive Triggers:**\n - Feature fully implemented and verified\n - Approach abandoned for alternative\n@@ -337,9 +377,61 @@ specs/022-hybrid-rag-fusion/        <- Coordination root (point-in-time snapshot\n     └── 002-skill-review/            <- Nested child\n ```\n \n+### Track With Sub-Tracks\n+\n+```\n+specs/billing/\n+├── description.json                 # level: \"track\"\n+├── graph-metadata.json              # children_ids: 001-invoices, invoicing\n+├── 001-invoices/\n+│   ├── spec.md\n+│   └── ...\n+├── invoicing/                       # declared sub-track\n+│   ├── description.json             # level: \"sub-track\"\n+│   ├── graph-metadata.json          # parent_id: billing\n+│   ├── 001-numbering/\n+│   │   ├── spec.md\n+│   │   └── ...\n+│   └── 002-credits/\n+└── z_archive/\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 7. HOST REPOSITORY TRIGGER INDEX\n+\n+The packaged index at `runtime/data/trigger-index.json` is the default every lookup reads. A host repository that vendors Skilled can build an index over its own docs at `.speckit-index/trigger-index.json`. Nothing selects that file on its own, so the host passes it with `--index`.\n+\n+Generate from the host root:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --repo-root . \\\n+  --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+```\n+\n+Call it from the host's Gate 1 lookup:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --index .speckit-index/trigger-index.json \\\n+  --json -- \"<prompt>\"\n+```\n+\n+Exit `0` means candidates, `1` a clean miss and `2` a bad invocation or an unreadable index. `--out` alone writes the corpus manifest, diagnostics and phrase variants beside the index. Check freshness against the same file:\n+\n+```bash\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --check \\\n+  --repo-root . \\\n+  --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+```\n+\n+Without `--index`, the lookup keeps reading the packaged index.\n+\n ---\n \n-## 7. RELATED RESOURCES\n+## 8. RELATED RESOURCES\n \n - [spec-kit-docs.json](../../templates/spec-kit-docs.json) - Level contract resolved by create.sh\n - [Template Guide](../templates/template-guide.md)\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && git diff ac32d66fed..7714ff26b1 -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/folder-structure.md | head -260\"}"},"time":{"start":1794075605292,"end":1794075607936}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794075607938,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b73d34a4001NfXroomKjSA66K","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b73c3602001aT5Xegmqr7ovg1","type":"tool","id":"call_adaedb6fef98485cbc99bbcd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && git diff ac32d66fed..7714ff26b1 -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/README.md .skilled/commands/speckit/search.md .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md | head -260"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md b/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\nindex 3b90d0ee09..8f56adc2e7 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@ The keyed lookup over the generated index. Reads a file and exits.\n node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<QUERY>\"\n ```\n \n+The default index is the packaged `runtime/data/trigger-index.json`. A host repository that generated its own index passes it explicitly: `--index .speckit-index/trigger-index.json`.\n+\n 1. Run the command with the resolved `QUERY`.\n 2. Branch on the exit status: `0` = candidates, `1` = clean no-hit, `2` or higher = the index is missing or unreadable.\n 3. Render candidates with the Section 2 contract in the presentation asset — score, match class and path, in the order the tool returned them.\n@@ -105,7 +107,7 @@ rg --no-config --hidden --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case \\\n   -- '<QUERY>' specs .skilled\n ```\n \n-1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by positional path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n+1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by positional path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>` for one declared sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>/<NNN-name>` for a packet inside a sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n 2. Run exactly one recipe. Never combine `--json` with the path-only or count mode: ripgrep does not reject the combination, the last output-mode flag wins silently, and a JSONL parser handed count output sees an empty result rather than an error.\n 3. Branch on the exit status: `0` = matches, `1` = no match returned as an empty result, `2` or higher = an execution or configuration error.\n 4. Order results with the ranking tuple in `retrieval-conventions.md` Section 5 — evidence field, then normalized match class, then relative path and one-based line. Ripgrep supplies matches, paths and lines; it never ranks relevance, and no rendered output may imply that it does.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md\nindex 867d3ea802..b5fc5e1184 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md\n@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"documentation levels\"\n   - \"memory save\"\n   - \"spec folder workflow\"\n-version: 2.7.27.0\n+version: 2.7.28.0\n ---\n \n # System Spec Kit\n@@ -240,6 +240,8 @@ specs/<track>/<###-feature-name>/\n \n The track folder itself, `specs/<track>/`, holds no spec docs. Its `graph-metadata.json` lists the track's packets in `children_ids`. `create.sh --track` adds each new packet to that list, `archive.sh` refreshes it after moving a packet into the track's own `z_archive/` or back, `refresh-track-roots.mjs --apply` rewrites it from the packet folders on disk, and the pre-push hook blocks a pushed commit whose list disagrees with the packets it holds.\n \n+A track can also hold one declared sub-track level, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>/<NNN-name>/`. A sub-track is a non-numbered child with no `spec.md`, `description.json` at level `sub-track` and the same `graph-metadata.json` shape as a track root, and the track lists it in `children_ids`. It numbers its own packets from `001`, keeps its own `z_archive/`, and is skipped with one diagnostic when it is a symlink. Undeclared non-numbered folders are reported, never promoted. One level only.\n+\n ### Documentation Levels\n \n Not every change needs the same amount of paperwork. A one-line bug fix does not need an architecture decision record. A multi-system refactor does. Four levels match documentation depth to task complexity:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/README.md\nindex 49d9547716..34119a1e21 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/README.md\n@@ -34,6 +34,26 @@ Current state:\n - Do not hand-edit the index; the generator is the only writer.\n - Do not place databases, logs, or large artifacts here.\n \n+### Host Repository Index\n+\n+A host repository that vendors Skilled keeps its own index at `.speckit-index/trigger-index.json` in the host root. Nothing selects that file automatically: the lookup's default stays the packaged `runtime/data/trigger-index.json`, so the host passes its path with `--index`.\n+\n+```bash\n+# generate from the host root\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --repo-root . --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+\n+# Gate 1 lookup against the host index\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --index .speckit-index/trigger-index.json --json -- \"<prompt>\"\n+\n+# freshness check against the same file\n+node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs \\\n+  --check --repo-root . --out .speckit-index/trigger-index.json\n+```\n+\n+`--out` alone writes the corpus manifest, diagnostics and phrase variants beside the index. Regenerate it after any `trigger_phrases` change in the host's docs.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md b/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\nindex 3b90d0ee09..8f56adc2e7 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@ The keyed lookup over the generated index. Reads a file and exits.\n node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json -- \"<QUERY>\"\n ```\n \n+The default index is the packaged `runtime/data/trigger-index.json`. A host repository that generated its own index passes it explicitly: `--index .speckit-index/trigger-index.json`.\n+\n 1. Run the command with the resolved `QUERY`.\n 2. Branch on the exit status: `0` = candidates, `1` = clean no-hit, `2` or higher = the index is missing or unreadable.\n 3. Render candidates with the Section 2 contract in the presentation asset — score, match class and path, in the order the tool returned them.\n@@ -105,7 +107,7 @@ rg --no-config --hidden --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case \\\n   -- '<QUERY>' specs .skilled\n ```\n \n-1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by positional path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for one packet, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>/<NNN-child-name>` for one phase child. `--packet <specFolder>` replaces the roots with that path.\n+1. Resolve the search roots. Narrow by positional path, never by pattern: `specs .skilled` for everything, `specs/<track>` for one track, `specs/<track>/<sub-track>` for one declared sub-track, `specs/<track>/<NNN-name>` for on