{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794076451435,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b74a1268001pFgW03azW9LvOJ","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b74972b5001m6UrrhGADAQlef","type":"tool","id":"call_810ebbe59117497d9c02fbf0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && ls specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/scratch/; echo \"---baseline---\"; cat specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/scratch/baseline.txt; echo \"---perf grep---\"; grep -rn \"0.04\\|0.05\\|track discovery\\|NFR-P01\" specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/scratch specs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/research 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"baseline-vitest.log\nbaseline.txt\nred-A.log\nred-B.log\nred-C.log\nred-D.log\nred-F.log\nred-G.log\nt019-reproduction.log\n---baseline---\n# Baseline 2026-11-07, HEAD 6ab6760362\n# vitest (from runtime/cli: --config ../../vitest.config.ts --project cli)\ntests/archive-track.vitest.ts pass=54 fail=0\ntests/create-root-numbering.vitest.ts pass=16 fail=0\ntests/create-track-containment.vitest.ts pass=10 fail=0\ntests/create-track-refresh.vitest.ts pass=11 fail=0\ntests/graph-metadata-refresh.vitest.ts pass=5 fail=0\ntests/repair-derived.vitest.ts pass=36 fail=0\ntests/track-roots.vitest.ts pass=10 fail=0\ntests/validate-recursive-artifact-skip.vitest.ts pass=3 fail=0\n# node --test doctor\nsymlink-engine.test.cjs pass=12 fail=0\ndoctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs pass=34 fail=0\n---perf grep---\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/scratch/red-D.log:25:✔ the unlink workflow is interactive and changes only recorded paths (0.048125ms)\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/scratch/red-D.log:30:✔ the doctor family contract names the symlink router and generic route assets (0.052458ms)\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/research/deep-research-audit-ledger/frames/0000000000000003.frame:1:{\"canonical_event_bytes\":\"\",\"canonical_event_hash\":\"1e362509808a5808ac8e652611578fc4e6cdaf801e6d0939e0fe95c1a34e4200\",\"decision_digest\":\"6fb083bfa96328fe0004591d7e339694cf492b21e5ca567912002c375d9e34d2\",\"frame_version\":1,\"ledger_id\":\"deep-research-audit-ledger\",\"prev_record_hash\":\"7713c549aab2d7b829e1119178b5eb8c90c5daa72b3bf39cbc5347e957f58bcf\",\"record_hash\":\"66d91e13b738de4fd052f0393c1a87d13d6408d206c5fbdd2cd3808f582473c3\",\"sequence\":3}\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/research/findings-registry.json:267:      \"text\": \"**Treat a sub-track as one extra container level in validation, refresh, create, and archive.** Recursive validation and track discovery currently enumerate only immediate numbered directories; the validator exempts a root only when its parent is named specs. Archive accepts numbered descendants beneath a track but rejects a named segment, and track_of only recognizes a packet directly under specs/<track>. A sub-track z_archive must be excluded from sub-track discovery and treated as that sub-track's archive. A numbered phase parent inside a sub-track remains one direct packet root in the sub-track's children_ids, with its numbered phases still owned by that parent. create.sh already chooses the next number from the selected SPECS_DIR, so per-sub-track numbering is supported by the current path selection; the slash-containing track value skips metadata refresh, which is the gap to close. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh:186] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh:315] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:219] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/run