3808f582473c3\",\"sequence\":3}\nspecs/system-speckit/spec-folder-tooling/002-named-subtracks-and-host-repos/research/findings-registry.json:267:      \"text\": \"**Treat a sub-track as one extra container level in validation, refresh, create, and archive.** Recursive validation and track discovery currently enumerate only immediate numbered directories; the validator exempts a root only when its parent is named specs. Archive accepts numbered descendants beneath a track but rejects a named segment, and track_of only recognizes a packet directly under specs/<track>. A sub-track z_archive must be excluded from sub-track discovery and treated as that sub-track's archive. A numbered phase parent inside a sub-track remains one direct packet root in the sub-track's children_ids, with its numbered phases still owned by that parent. create.sh already chooses the next number from the selected SPECS_DIR, so per-sub-track numbering is supported by the current path selection; the slash-containing track value skips metadata refresh, which is the gap to close. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh:186] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh:315] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:219] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:221] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/validation/orchestrator.ts:1340] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:189] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:207] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh:219] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:1012] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:1306] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:1463] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh:1474] [SOURCE: .sk