| `local` | A real file or folder with no links into the checkout |\n105:With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the entries with their own status and detail, the detected runtimes, the tracked absolute links and whether the root is a git work tree.\n115:Evidence: [n] entries, [n] linked-whole, [n] linked-merge, [n] partial-merge, [n] missing, [n] broken, [n] foreign-link, [n] local, [n] source-missing, [n] tracked absolute links\n296:| An entry reports `foreign-link` | The name points at another checkout or another file, so every run refuses it. Decide which checkout belongs at that name before anything changes |\n298:| An entry reports `local` | The name is the repository's own file or folder. Nothing is overwritten. Where the name is a real folder, `--mode merge` puts links inside it and keeps every local path |\n301:| A refusal names a real file | The name is the repository's own file. A link would replace it, so nothing is written. Rename the local file, or leave the name alone |\n303:| Ignore lines went somewhere the team does not see | `--ignore exclude` writes to `<git-dir>/info/exclude`, which is local to this clone. Use `--ignore gitignore` to write `.gitignore` when the team wants them shared |\n309:| `--include env` warns about secrets | The run links the checkout's `.env`, so every tool started in that repository reads the Skilled secrets. Drop `env` from `--include` to keep them local to the checkout |\n321:| The operator wants the whole setup walked through in order | `/doctor:install` | It prints the ordered writing checklist for a new project repository |\n---tests helper findEntry---\n126:function findEntry(report, name) {\n127-  const pending = [report];\n128-  while (pending.length > 0) {\n129-    const value = pending.pop();\n130-    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n131-      pending.push(...value);\n132-    } else if (value && typeof value === 'object') {\n133-      if (value.name === name && typeof value.status === 'string') return value;\n134-      pending.push(...Object.values(value));\n135-    }\n136-  }\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"7:Every argument failure happens before any workflow YAML loads, prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, and ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n52:Give the path to the project repo that should hold the links. This command never links the Skilled checkout into itself.\n74:2. No real file and no real folder is ever overwritten. A name that holds a real file is refused. A real folder gets links built inside it, and the local paths inside it are kept. A real folder is never replaced by a link.\n75:3. Only a broken link whose text points into the Skilled checkout is replaced or removed. A link that points somewhere else is reported `foreign-link` and left exactly as it is.\n81:The engine prints one human line per entry, `<status> <group> <name>`, with indented detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts, then the repository-level warnings. Quote the lines rather than paraphrasing them, and lead the reply with the entries that are not linked as asked.\n83:A row is a pass only when it reads `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. Every other status is a row to show in full:\n87:| `linked-whole` | The name is a link to the checkout, as asked |\n92:| `foreign-link` | A link that resolves somewhere other than the checkout |\n93:| `local` | A real file or folder with no links into the checkout |\n105:With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the entries with their own status and detail, the detected runtimes, the tracked absolute links and whether the root is a git work tree.\n115:Evidence: [n] entries, [n] linked-whole, [n] linked-merge, [n] partial-merge, [n] missing, [n] broken, [n] foreign-link, [n] local, [n] source-missing, [n] tracked absolute links\n296:| An entry reports `foreign-link` | The name points at another checkout or another file, so every run refuses it. Decide which checkout belongs at that name before anything changes |\n298:| An entry reports `local` | The name is the repository's own file or folder. Nothing is overwritten. Where the name is a real folder, `--mode merge` puts links inside it and keeps every local path |\n301:| A refusal names a real file | The name is the repository's own file. A link would replace it, so nothing is written. Rename the local file, or leave the name alone |\n303:| Ignore lines went somewhere the team does not see | `--ignore exclude` writes to `<git-dir>/info/exclude`, which is local to this clone. Use `--ignore gitignore` to write `.gitignore` when the team wants them shared |\n309:| `--include env` warns about secrets | The run links the checkout's `.env`, so every tool started in that repository reads the Skilled secrets. Drop `env` from `--include` to keep them local to the checkout |\n321:| The operator wants the whole setup walked through in order | `/doctor:install` | It prints the ordered writing checklist for a new project repository |\n---tests helper findEntry---\n126:function findEntry(report, name) {\n127-  const pending = [report];\n128-  while (pending.length > 0) {\n129-    const value = pending.pop();\n130-    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n131-      pending.push(...value);\n132-    } else if (value && typeof value === 'object') {\n133-      if (value.name === name && typeof value.status === 'string') return value;\n134-      pending.push(...Object.values(value));\n135-    }\n136-  }\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -n \\\"linked-whole\\\\|local\\\\|foreign\\\\|status\\\\|project\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.