{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794076686616,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b74db48a0027d7GG5IrVpPKMl","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b74d61d2001FUceZHNMZWIf7s","type":"tool","id":"call_ee3b8d32460c4fbb94b93a40","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && sed -n '78,120p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt; echo \"---engine check exit---\"; grep -n \"function check\\|exitCode\\|process.exit\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs | tail -30"},"output":"\n## 4. Check Report\n\nThe engine prints one human line per entry, `<status> <group> <name>`, with indented detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts, then the repository-level warnings. Quote the lines rather than paraphrasing them, and lead the reply with the entries that are not linked as asked.\n\nA row is a pass only when it reads `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. Every other status is a row to show in full:\n\n| Status | What it means |\n|--------|---------------|\n| `linked-whole` | The name is a link to the checkout, as asked |\n| `linked-merge` | A real folder whose entries link into the checkout, with no broken link into it |\n| `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some entries, or holding broken links into the checkout |\n| `missing` | Nothing sits at that name |\n| `broken` | A link whose target does not exist |\n| `foreign-link` | A link that resolves somewhere other than the checkout |\n| `local` | A real file or folder with no links into the checkout |\n| `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path, so nothing can be linked |\n\n```text\nSkilled link check: [the root the engine read]\n\n[one line per entry, as the engine printed it]\n[indented detail lines, as printed]\n[repository-level warnings, as printed, including each tracked absolute link]\nSTATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n```\n\nWith `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the entries with their own status and detail, the detected runtimes, the tracked absolute links and whether the root is a git work tree.\n\n### Check Summary\n\n```text\nDOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\nTarget: check\nStatus: [OK|FINDINGS|FAIL]\nMutation class: read-only\nScope: [the root the engine read]\nEvidence: [n] entries, [n] linked-whole, [n] linked-merge, [n] partial-merge, [n] missing, [n] broken, [n] foreign-link, [n] local, [n] source-missing, [n] tracked absolute links\nRecommendation: [the repair each non-pass entry needs, or none]\nSTATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n```\n\n`STATUS=OK` covers a check that ran, and the rows and the summary carry the findings. `Status: FINDINGS` holds when at least one selected entry is not a pass or a tracked absolute link printed, and `Status: OK` holds when every selected entry is a pass. An engine exit 2 ends `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[the engine's code]\"`, and the reply names the accepted invocation.\n---engine check exit---\n1798:  process.exitCode = main(process.argv.slice(2));\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## 4. Check Report\n\nThe engine prints one human line per entry, `<status> <group> <name>`, with indented detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts, then the repository-level warnings. Quote the lines rather than paraphrasing them, and lead the reply with the entries that are not linked as asked.\n\nA row is a pass only when it reads `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. Every other status is a row to show in full:\n\n| Status | What it means |\n|--------|---------------|\n| `linked-whole` | The name is a link to the checkout, as asked |\n| `linked-merge` | A real folder whose entries link into the checkout, with no broken link into it |\n| `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some entries, or holding broken links into the checkout |\n| `missing` | Nothing sits at that name |\n| `broken` | A link whose target does not exist |\n| `foreign-link` | A link that resolves somewhere other than the checkout |\n| `local` | A real file or folder with no links into the checkout |\n| `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path, so nothing can be linked |\n\n```text\nSkilled link check: [the root the engine read]\n\n[one line per entry, as the engine printed it]\n[indented detail lines, as printed]\n[repository-level warnings, as printed, including each tracked absolute link]\nSTATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n```\n\nWith `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the entries with their own status and detail, the detected runtimes, the tracked absolute links and whether the root is a git work tree.\n\n### Check Summary\n\n```text\nDOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\nTarget: check\nStatus: [OK|FINDINGS|FAIL]\nMutation class: read-only\nScope: [the root the engine read]\nEvidence: [n] entries, [n] linked-whole, [n] linked-merge, [n] partial-merge, [n] missing, [n] broken, [n] foreign-link, [n] local, [n] source-missing, [n] tracked absolute links\nRecommendation: [the repair each non-pass entry needs, or none]\nSTATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n```\n\n`STATUS=OK` covers a check that ran, and the rows and the summary carry the findings. `Status: FINDINGS` holds when at least one selected entry is not a pass or a tracked absolute link printed, and `Status: OK` holds when every selected entry is a pass. An engine exit 2 ends `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[the engine's code]\"`, and the reply names the accepted invocation.\n---engine check exit---\n1798:  process.exitCode = main(process.argv.slice(2));\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && sed -n '78,120p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt; echo \\\"---engine check exit---\\\"; grep -n \\\"function check\\\\|exitCode\\\\|process.exit\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs | tail -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794076685450,"end":1794076686616}}}}
