{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794076742139,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b74e8d8d0015GpMEv6SmkPjwr","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b74e22a40012it1aQBy6zNIiZ","type":"tool","id":"call_9a64290b78c249b5ae031f04","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && sed -n '1,160p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml"},"output":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\npurpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\naction: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\nskill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single_step_check\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: true\n  allowed_targets: []\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"**/*\"\n  invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n  manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n  presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninputs:\n  execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n  root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n  source: \"Optional Skilled checkout path, passed as --source <dir>. When omitted, the engine resolves its checkout root from its own script path.\"\n  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n  include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n  link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n  json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n  target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EXECUTION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nexecution:\n  steps:\n    - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n    - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --source \"{source}\" when supplied, --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n    - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n    - \"Exit 0 means the check ran. Findings are part of its report, not a failure code. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n    - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput: |\n  STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n  STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\npurpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\naction: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\nskill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single_step_check\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: true\n  allowed_targets: []\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"**/*\"\n  invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n  manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n  presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninputs:\n  execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n  root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n  source: \"Optional Skilled checkout path, passed as --source <dir>. When omitted, the engine resolves its checkout root from its own script path.\"\n  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n  include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n  link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n  json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n  target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EXECUTION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nexecution:\n  steps:\n    - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n    - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --source \"{source}\" when supplied, --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n    - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n    - \"Exit 0 means the check ran. Findings are part of its report, not a failure code. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n    - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput: |\n  STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n  STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && sed -n '1,160p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794076741005,"end":1794076742139}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794076742143,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b74e8488001tlRoB9QG5lenSC","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b74e22a40012it1aQBy6zNIiZ","type":"tool","id":"call_c7321b79463f40598f17c96e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -n \"linked-whole\\|linked-merge\\|project\\|status\\|pass\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml | head -60; echo \"---routes---\"; grep -n \"symlink\" -A20 .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -80"},"output":"5:purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n43:  root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n44:  source: \"Optional Skilled checkout path, passed as --source <dir>. When omitted, the engine resolves its checkout root from its own script path.\"\n45:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:  include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:  link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:  json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n58:    - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n---routes---\n21:#   /doctor:symlink         .skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md\n22-#   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23-#   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24-# A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25-# Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26-# Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27-#   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28-#   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29-#   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30-#   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31-#   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32-#   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33-#\n34-# Schema (per route):\n35-#   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36-#   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37-#   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38-#   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39-#   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40-#   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41-#   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n--\n543:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n544-    target: check\n545-    default_target: true\n546:    yaml: doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n547-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, include, link_instructions, json_output]\n548-    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\", \"--include <list>\", \"--link-instructions\"]\n549-    mutating: read-only\n550-    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; the engine classifies every framework entry in the target repository and writes nothing)\"\n551-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n552-    script_invocations:\n553:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes, --include, --link-instructions and --json only when the operator passed them'\n554-    trigger_phrases:\n555:      - \"check skilled symlinks in a repo\"\n556:      - \"find broken skilled symlinks\"\n557-      - \"which runtime folders are linked\"\n558-      - \"is skilled linked into my project\"\n559-      - \"the skilled links are broken\"\n560-      - \"broken skilled links in my project\"\n561-      - \"skilled links in my project\"\n562-\n563:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n564-    target: link\n565:    yaml: doctor-symlink-link.yaml\n566-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, mode, include, link_instructions, ignore, dry_run, plan_digest, digest_confirmation]\n567-    allowed_flags: [\"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\", \"--mode <shape>\", \"--include <list>\", \"--link-instructions\", \"--ignore <where>\", \"--dry-run\", \"--plan-digest <digest>\"]\n568-    mutating: mutates\n569:    gate3_location: \"the target repository's framework links (whole-folder links, or real folders holding one link per entry), the broken links into the Skilled checkout that the plan replaces or removes, and the ignore lines in <git-dir>/info/exclude (or .gitignore behind --ignore gitignore), with the run record written to the checkout's .skilled/output/doctor-symlink/<first 16 hex of the digest>/manifest.json, or the next free <prefix>-2, <prefix>-3 folder when an earlier run holds it, before the first action; no real file or folder is ever overwritten, and the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n570-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n571-    script_invocations:\n572:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs plan --root <dir>  # read-only: prints every action, every refusal and the plan digest; the workflow adds --runtimes, --mode, --include, --link-instructions and --ignore only when the operator passed them'\n573:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs apply --root <dir> --plan-digest <digest>  # recomposes with the same flags, refuses a digest that no longer matches, records the run, applies the actions and reruns check; the workflow runs it only after the operator approves the plan that printed that digest'\n574-    trigger_phrases:\n575:      - \"symlink skilled into my project\"\n576-      - \"link the claude folder into my repo\"\n577:      - \"repair broken skilled symlinks\"\n578-      - \"create the skilled links in a repo\"\n579-      - \"link skilled into my repo\"\n580-      - \"link skilled into another project\"\n581-      - \"link my skilled checkout into another project\"\n582-\n583:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n584-    target: unlink\n585:    yaml: doctor-symlink-unlink.yaml\n586-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, run_dir, yes, dry_run]\n587-    allowed_flags: [\"--run <dir>\", \"--yes\", \"--dry-run\"]\n588-    mutating: mutates\n589-    gate3_location: \"only the links, the folders and the ignore lines one run's manifest.json records, each re-checked against the recorded state before it is touched; a path that changed since the apply is skipped and reported, and the run directory itself is read and kept\"\n590-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n591-    script_invocations:\n592:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --dry-run  # prints what the unlink would remove or restore and writes nothing'\n593:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --yes  # removes the recorded links and empty folders and the recorded ignore lines; the workflow passes --yes only after its own yes'\n594-    trigger_phrases:\n595:      - \"undo a skilled symlink run\"\n596:      - \"remove the skilled symlinks again\"\n597-      - \"unlink skilled from my project\"\n598-\n599-  - command: /doctor:install\n600-    target: guide\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5:purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n43:  root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n44:  source: \"Optional Skilled checkout path, passed as --source <dir>. When omitted, the engine resolves its checkout root from its own script path.\"\n45:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:  include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:  link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:  json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n58:    - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n---routes---\n21:#   /doctor:symlink         .skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md\n22-#   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23-#   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24-# A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25-# Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26-# Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27-#   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28-#   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29-#   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30-#   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31-#   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32-#   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33-#\n34-# Schema (per route):\n35-#   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36-#   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37-#   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38-#   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39-#   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40-#   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41-#   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n--\n543:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n544-    target: check\n545-    default_target: true\n546:    yaml: doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n547-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, include, link_instructions, json_output]\n548-    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\", \"--include <list>\", \"--link-instructions\"]\n549-    mutating: read-only\n550-    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only diagnostic; the engine classifies every framework entry in the target repository and writes nothing)\"\n551-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n552-    script_invocations:\n553:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes, --include, --link-instructions and --json only when the operator passed them'\n554-    trigger_phrases:\n555:      - \"check skilled symlinks in a repo\"\n556:      - \"find broken skilled symlinks\"\n557-      - \"which runtime folders are linked\"\n558-      - \"is skilled linked into my project\"\n559-      - \"the skilled links are broken\"\n560-      - \"broken skilled links in my project\"\n561-      - \"skilled links in my project\"\n562-\n563:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n564-    target: link\n565:    yaml: doctor-symlink-link.yaml\n566-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, mode, include, link_instructions, ignore, dry_run, plan_digest, digest_confirmation]\n567-    allowed_flags: [\"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\", \"--mode <shape>\", \"--include <list>\", \"--link-instructions\", \"--ignore <where>\", \"--dry-run\", \"--plan-digest <digest>\"]\n568-    mutating: mutates\n569:    gate3_location: \"the target repository's framework links (whole-folder links, or real folders holding one link per entry), the broken links into the Skilled checkout that the plan replaces or removes, and the ignore lines in <git-dir>/info/exclude (or .gitignore behind --ignore gitignore), with the run record written to the checkout's .skilled/output/doctor-symlink/<first 16 hex of the digest>/manifest.json, or the next free <prefix>-2, <prefix>-3 folder when an earlier run holds it, before the first action; no real file or folder is ever overwritten, and the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n570-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n571-    script_invocations:\n572:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs plan --root <dir>  # read-only: prints every action, every refusal and the plan digest; the workflow adds --runtimes, --mode, --include, --link-instructions and --ignore only when the operator passed them'\n573:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs apply --root <dir> --plan-digest <digest>  # recomposes with the same flags, refuses a digest that no longer matches, records the run, applies the actions and reruns check; the workflow runs it only after the operator approves the plan that printed that digest'\n574-    trigger_phrases:\n575:      - \"symlink skilled into my project\"\n576-      - \"link the claude folder into my repo\"\n577:      - \"repair broken skilled symlinks\"\n578-      - \"create the skilled links in a repo\"\n579-      - \"link skilled into my repo\"\n580-      - \"link skilled into another project\"\n581-      - \"link my skilled checkout into another project\"\n582-\n583:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n584-    target: unlink\n585:    yaml: doctor-symlink-unlink.yaml\n586-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, run_dir, yes, dry_run]\n587-    allowed_flags: [\"--run <dir>\", \"--yes\", \"--dry-run\"]\n588-    mutating: mutates\n589-    gate3_location: \"only the links, the folders and the ignore lines one run's manifest.json records, each re-checked against the recorded state before it is touched; a path that changed since the apply is skipped and reported, and the run directory itself is read and kept\"\n590-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n591-    script_invocations:\n592:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --dry-run  # prints what the unlink would remove or restore and writes nothing'\n593:      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <dir> --yes  # removes the recorded links and empty folders and the recorded ignore lines; the workflow passes --yes only after its own yes'\n594-    trigger_phrases:\n595:      - \"undo a skilled symlink run\"\n596:      - \"remove the skilled symlinks again\"\n597-      - \"unlink skilled from my project\"\n598-\n599-  - command: /doctor:install\n600-    target: guide\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -n \\\"linked-whole\\\\|linked-merge\\\\|project\\\\|status\\\\|pass\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml | head -60; echo \\\"---routes---\\\"; grep -n \\\"symlink\\\" -A20 .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -80\"}"},"time":{"start":1794076738696,"end":17940