{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794078176621,"sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","part":{"partID":"prt_1b7646e81001VhlhsguFHtQKlr","sessionID":"ses_e48de3ad0ffeE5McT5ooWqWS7z","messageID":"msg_1b76422e2001o2P8uubKITXHvw","type":"tool","id":"call_24a2af66fb3946c0ab7e0ba0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -n \"record.run\\|const run\\|run = \\|run:\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs | head -40; echo \"---state-jsonl iteration example---\"; grep -n \"iteration record\\|\\\"type\\\": \\\"iteration\\\"\\|type.*iteration\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md | head -20; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md | head -80"},"output":"296:function parseFindingsBlock(sectionText, severity, run = 0) {\n339:  const runMatch = iterationPath.match(/iteration-(\\d+)\\.md$/);\n357:  const run = runMatch ? Number(runMatch[1]) : 0;\n368:    run: runMatch ? Number(runMatch[1]) : 0,\n459:    const run = isFiniteNumber(getNestedField(record, 'run'))\n680:  if (isFiniteNumber(record.run)) {\n681:    return record.run;\n683:  const runText = normalizeText(record.run || '');\n684:  const runMatch = runText.match(/(\\d+)$/);\n732:  const run = getIterationRun(record) || 0;\n763:    const run = getIterationRun(record);\n1006:    const run = isFiniteNumber(record.iteration) ? record.iteration : 0;\n1018:  for (const run of sortedRuns) {\n1042:    const run = getIterationRun(record);\n1356:      sourceIteration: isFiniteNumber(record.run) ? record.run : null,\n1465:        run: isFiniteNumber(getNestedField(record, 'run')) ? getNestedField(record, 'run') : 0,\n1545:    const iteration = Number.isFinite(record.iteration) ? record.iteration : record.run;\n1918:  const runningFindings = [\n---state-jsonl iteration example---\n63:  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n95:**Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n131:  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n176:4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n416:| `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n437:  \"type\": \"iteration\",\n465:| v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | A validator may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n---\ntitle: Deep Review State Log Records\ndescription: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n  - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n  - \"review depth schema\"\n  - \"review traceability checks\"\n  - \"review graph events\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.2.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Log Records\n\nOpen this when you are writing or auditing `deep-review-state.jsonl`, the append-only source of truth for a review run, and need the record shape the reducer expects.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n- Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n- Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n- Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n\n### Key Sources\n\n| Source | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n| Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n| Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n| Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n\nAppend-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n\nWhile the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n\n### Line 1: Config Record\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n```\n\nThe projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n\n### Iteration Records\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n  \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"findingsCount\": 4,\n  \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n  \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n  \"findingDetails\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"296:function parseFindingsBlock(sectionText, severity, run = 0) {\n339:  const runMatch = iterationPath.match(/iteration-(\\d+)\\.md$/);\n357:  const run = runMatch ? Number(runMatch[1]) : 0;\n368:    run: runMatch ? Number(runMatch[1]) : 0,\n459:    const run = isFiniteNumber(getNestedField(record, 'run'))\n680:  if (isFiniteNumber(record.run)) {\n681:    return record.run;\n683:  const runText = normalizeText(record.run || '');\n684:  const runMatch = runText.match(/(\\d+)$/);\n732:  const run = getIterationRun(record) || 0;\n763:    const run = getIterationRun(record);\n1006:    const run = isFiniteNumber(record.iteration) ? record.iteration : 0;\n1018:  for (const run of sortedRuns) {\n1042:    const run = getIterationRun(record);\n1356:      sourceIteration: isFiniteNumber(record.run) ? record.run : null,\n1465:        run: isFiniteNumber(getNestedField(record, 'run')) ? getNestedField(record, 'run') : 0,\n1545:    const iteration = Number.isFinite(record.iteration) ? record.iteration : record.run;\n1918:  const runningFindings = [\n---state-jsonl iteration example---\n63:  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n95:**Required fields:** `type`, `mode`, `iteration`, `status`, `focus`, `dimensions`, `filesReviewed`, `findingsCount`, `findingsSummary`, `findingsNew`, `findingDetails`, `newFindingsRatio`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `lineageMode`, `timestamp`, `durationMs`\n131:  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 4, \"status\": \"complete\",\n176:4. **Persistence gate**: the reducer refuses to roll graph events forward when a record is missing `sessionId` on the surrounding iteration record, because the DB cannot route the write.\n416:| `id` | string | Yes | Stable ledger-row id unique within the iteration record. |\n437:  \"type\": \"iteration\",\n465:| v1 legacy: discriminator absent or not `2` | Parse as today's iteration record. | A validator may warn, but must not hard-fail only because v2 fields are absent. |\n---\ntitle: Deep Review State Log Records\ndescription: JSONL state-log record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema v2 for the deep review loop.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review state jsonl\"\n  - \"review jsonl record schemas\"\n  - \"review depth schema\"\n  - \"review traceability checks\"\n  - \"review graph events\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.2.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review State Log Records\n\nOpen this when you are writing or auditing `deep-review-state.jsonl`, the append-only source of truth for a review run, and need the record shape the reducer expects.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis reference defines the append-only JSONL records that preserve deep-review run state. It covers config, iteration, event, lineage, graph, verdict, traceability, and Review Depth Schema v2 records so reducers and validators can replay the loop deterministically.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Validating `deep-review-state.jsonl` shape before changing reducers, dashboards, or workflow emission.\n- Debugging malformed state records, blocked-stop events, graph convergence events, or lineage fields.\n- Adding or checking Review Depth Schema v2 target selection, search coverage, and ledger fields.\n- Confirming which fields are required before writing iteration, synthesis, pause, or recovery events.\n\n### Key Sources\n\n| Source | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| Config record | Establishes session identity, lineage, thresholds, and spec folder routing. |\n| Iteration record | Captures focus, reviewed files, findings, convergence ratios, and graph events. |\n| Event records | Persist synthesis, blocked-stop, graph convergence, pause, and stuck-recovery decisions. |\n| Review Depth Schema v2 | Adds target selection, search coverage, and ledger proof for deeper review iterations. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. STATE LOG (DEEP-REVIEW-STATE.JSONL)\n\nAppend-only JSON Lines file. One JSON object per line.\n\nWhile the mode's authority record still names the legacy writer (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`), this file is the authoritative target the workflow appends to and no ledger backs it. Once that record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger becomes authoritative and the append gateway refreshes this file as a projection of it. The projection folds only the registered stems, and a refresh that would replace an existing config row while dropping any of its keys is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` before any bytes are written. The registered stems, the producer census, and what a refresh can and cannot reproduce are in `state-format.md` section 11.\n\n### Line 1: Config Record\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"config\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"topic\":\"...\",\"reviewTarget\":\"...\",\"sessionId\":\"rvw-...\",\"parentSessionId\":null,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"continuedFromRun\":null,\"maxIterations\":7,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.10,\"createdAt\":\"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\"specFolder\":\"...\"}\n```\n\nThe projected variant of this row is thin: only `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, and `timestamp` come back from a ledger refresh. The remaining keys exist only in the row the workflow writes at init.\n\n### Iteration Records\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"iteration\", \"mode\": \"review\", \"iteration\": 3, \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"focus\": \"D3 Traceability - skill/runtime alignment\",\n  \"dimensions\": [\"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n  \"filesReviewed\": [\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/README.md\"],\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"findingsCount\": 4,\n  \"findingsSummary\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 3 },\n  \"findingsNew\": { \"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 1 },\n  \"findingDetails\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"Missing consumer update\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled && grep -n \\\"record.run\\\\|const run\\\\|run = \\\\|run:\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs | head -40; echo \\\"---state-jsonl iteration example---\\\"; grep -n \\\"iteration record\\\\|\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"iteration\\\\\\\"\\\\|type.*iteration\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md | head -20; sed -n '1,120p' .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md | head -80\"}"},"time":{"start":1794078174849,"end":1794078176621}}}}
